<div class="exercise-info">
    <h1>Exercise Name: Seated Leg Extension (Toes-In Variant)</h1>
    <u><b><h4>Exercise Overview</h4></b></u>

This 3D anatomical animation demonstrates the Seated Leg Extension with Toes Pointed Inward ("toes in"). The video highlights how internal rotation of the feet shifts primary muscle activation onto the outer quadriceps (Vastus Lateralis), providing targeted isolation for the outer thigh.


 Exercise Name: Seated Leg Extension (Toes-In Variant)
 Target Muscles: Outer Quadriceps (Vastus Lateralis)
 Secondary Muscles: Inner and Center Quadriceps (Vastus Medialis, Rectus Femoris, Vastus Intermedius)
</div></div>
<pre>

<h1>How to Perform (Step-by-Step)</h1>
 <u><b><h4>Machine Setup</h4></b></u>: Adjust the back pad so your lower back rests firmly against it and your knees align with the machine’s pivot axis. Position the shin pad so it rests comfortably above your ankles.
 <u><b><h4>Foot Position</h4></b></u>: Turn your feet inward slightly at the ankles so your toes point toward each other ("toes in").
 <u><b><h4>Lifting Phase</h4></b></u>: Hold the side handles tightly to anchor your hips down. Exhale as you extend your legs upward in a smooth, controlled movement until your legs are nearly straight.
 <u><b><h4>Lowering Phase</h4></b></u>: Pause for a brief moment at the peak, squeeze your outer quads, and inhale as you lower the weight back down slowly.



<h1>Key Benefits</h1>

 <b>◉Outer Quad Isolation:</b> Shifts load specifically onto the Vastus Lateralis, helping build broad, defined outer thigh sweep.
 <b>◉Balanced Leg Development:</b> Complements standard and toes-out extensions to ensure proportional muscle development across all quad heads.
 <b>◉Targeted Knee Support:</b> Strengthens the lateralquadriceps complex to support overall knee joint mechanics.



<h1>Recommended Sets & Reps</h1>

| Goal | Sets | Reps | Rest |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Muscle Building (Hypertrophy) | 3 – 4 | 10 – 12 | 60 – 90 seconds |
| Endurance / Definition | 3 – 4 | 12 – 15 | 45 – 60 seconds |
| Strength | 3 – 4 | 8 – 10 | 90 seconds |

Keep foot rotation moderate (roughly 15–20 degrees inward) to target the outer quad safely without straining your knee joints or ankles.

